# .dockerignore
# Development and CI
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
*.md
LICENSE
Makefile

# Build artifacts
bin/
dist/
vendor/
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out

# Test artifacts
coverage*.out
test-results/
*.log

# Deployments and configs we don't need in test image
deployments/
build/docker/frontend/
build/docker/backend/
!build/docker/backend/github-actions-runner-entrypoint.sh
frontends/
docs/
# EXCEPT the `?` adoption-gate acks list, which optional-explicit-wires-check
# ships INSIDE its image (RFC_029 §10.15). It has to travel with the binary for
# the reason shared-output-fields-check keeps its ack list in scripts/: the acks
# are the check's own definition of "already known", so a ConfigMap or a
# working-tree build could carry an unreviewed acknowledgement — a silenced
# finding with no diff. It lives under docs/ rather than scripts/ because three
# other lanes' migrations already cite that path and because its sibling ledger
# (RFC_022's optional_key_budget_acks.json) lives there; un-ignoring one file is
# cheaper than moving a path other sessions reference. The alternative — mirroring
# it into a literal the job carries — is the exact drift trap CLAUDE.md records
# against 099/check.py.
!docs/agent_docs/docs024_key_docs_latest/architecture_review/optional_explicit_wire_acks.json
# Same argument, second gate: commit-sha-exposure-check (WFA-022, the standing
# form of migration 537's guard, bugs_closed/334) ships its own exceptions file
# the same way. ⚠ A NEW ack-shipping check needs a line HERE as well as in its
# dockerfile — without one the COPY fails at build time, which is the loud
# direction and how this line got written; the quiet direction would be worse.
!docs/agent_docs/docs024_key_docs_latest/architecture_review/commit_sha_exposure_acks.json
scripts/migration/
scripts/deployment/

# Temporary files
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# Large directories we definitely don't need
node_modules/
tests/  # The wrong directory if it exists
